Both tickets in scope are boundary / off-by-one bugs in pure logic functions with no external
dependencies, no I/O, and no UI layer. An AC is sufficient for such a bug only when it pins the
exact boundary value and asserts the expected behaviour on BOTH sides of that boundary
(e.g. age 64 vs age 65, or the last stop in the list vs the second-to-last). An AC that says
"seniors get the concession fare" without naming the boundary age is enrichable; an AC that
does not mention the boundary at all is insufficient.

